ransientRetry`, `TestTransientPushLanded`, `TestTransientExhausted`, the code and init lanes) are unaffected.\n- Run `make lint test`.\n- Failure case: the mutation in step 3 must make the test fail.\n- Edge case: the context is already cancelled when `Push` returns, so check that no step between the failed push and `transientWait` uses ctx in a way that returns a different error. For example, a landed-check fetch on retry runs only after the wait. If the test shows an error other than `context.Canceled`, assert on `errors.Is(err, context.Canceled)` only and note it in the PR.\n\n### Risk\nLow. Test-only change in one file. No production code, public interface, migration, or concurrency change. No protected path from `merge.protected_paths` is touched.\n\n### Size\nS. Files touched: `internal/committer/transient_test.go` (about 10 changed lines).\nEOF\ncat > .ard/440/triage-engineer.md <<'EOF'\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nMakes the flaky test cancel its context from inside the `flaky` test double on the first transient push failure, rather than on a wall-clock timer, so cancellation always lands in the backoff wait. The plan has three steps, all in one test file. Size S, risk low.\n\n## Open issues\nNone.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":557,"cache_read_input_tokens":13800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":557},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a14f355-0ae9-46d5-98b0-2e53b2ffc431","uuid":"065bf740-fcd4-44f4-b53e-b50446e4e552","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:44:30.113Z","request_id":"req_011ChQJG39nAr8YW2XufNe5W"}
